      "text": "To determine the day of the week for December 23, we start by noting that Thanksgiving is on Thursday, November 23. Therefore, the number of days between Thanksgiving and December 23 is calculated as follows:\n\n\\[\n12 - 23 + 1 = 10 \\text{ days}\n\\]\n\nNext, we need to determine what day of the week it will be 10 days after Thursday. We do this by finding the remainder when 10 is divided by 7 (since there are 7 days in a week):\n\n\\[\n10 \\div 7 = 1 \\text{ remainder } 3\n\\]\n\nThis means that 10 days after Thursday is 3 days after Thursday. Counting forward from Thursday:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Thursday} \\rightarrow \\text{Friday} \\rightarrow \\text{Saturday} \\rightarrow \\text{Sunday} \\rightarrow \\text{Monday} \\rightarrow \\text{Tuesday} \\rightarrow \\text{Wednesday} \\rightarrow \\text{Thursday} \\rightarrow \\text{Friday} \\rightarrow \\text{Saturday}\n\\]\n\nWe see that 3 days after Thursday is Saturday. Therefore, December 23 falls on a \\(\\boxed{\\text{Saturday}}\\).",
