      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To determine the day of the week for December 23 given that Thanksgiving (October 1st) is on Thursday, let's break down the problem step by step:\n\n1. **Identify the date and day of the week for Thanksgiving:**\n   - Thanksgiving: Thursday, November 23, 2019.\n\n2. **Count the number of days from November 23 to December 23:**\n   - November has 30 days.\n   - From November 23 to November 30, there are \\( 30 - 23 + 1 = 8 \\) days.\n   - December 1 to December 23 is \\( 23 - 1 + 1 = 23 \\) days.\n\n3. **Calculate the total number of days from November 23 to December 23:**\n   \\[\n   8 \\text{ (November days)} + 23 \\text{ (December days)} = 31 \\text{ days}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Determine the position of December 23 in the week:**\n   - We need to find the day of the week 31 days after a Thursday.\n   - A week has 7 days, so we calculate the remaining days after completing full weeks:\n     \\[\n     31 \\div 7 = 4 \\text{ weeks and } 3 \\text{ days remainder}\n     \\]\n   - This means 31 days is equivalent to 4 full weeks and 3 extra days.\n\n5. **Calculate the final day of the week:**\n   - Starting from Thursday (day 0), adding 3 days gives:\n     \\[\n     0 + 3 = 3\n     \\]\n   - The day 3 corresponds to:\n     - Day 1: Friday\n     - Day 2: Saturday\n     - Day 3: Sunday\n\nTherefore, December 23, 2019, falls on a \\(\\boxed{\\text{Sunday}}\\) day.",
