      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To determine the day of the week for December 23, given that Thanksgiving is on Thursday, November 23, we need to count the number of days between November 23 and December 23 and then find out which day of the week December 23 falls on based on that count.\n\nFirst, let's calculate the number of days between November 23 and December 23. This period spans 30 days.\n\nNext, we need to figure out the day of the week after 30 days from November 23. We do this by finding the remainder when 30 is divided by 7 (since there are 7 days in a week). This is because the days of the week repeat every 7 days.\n\n\\[ 30 \\div 7 = 4 \\text{ remainder } 2 \\]\n\nThis means that 30 days is equivalent to 4 full weeks and 2 extra days. Starting from Thursday (the day of November 23), we count 2 days forward:\n\n- November 23 is Thursday\n- November 24 is Friday\n- November 25 is Saturday\n- November 26 is Sunday\n- November 27 is Monday\n- November 28 is Tuesday\n- November 29 is Wednesday\n- November 30 is Thursday\n- December 1 is Friday\n- December 2 is Saturday\n- December 3 is Sunday\n- December 4 is Monday\n- December 5 is Tuesday\n- December 6 is Wednesday\n- December 7 is Thursday\n\nSo, December 23 is a \\(\\boxed{\\text{Sunday}}\\).",
